From 6f4fc2b6a2f6823a258e852c261503fd45848133 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Tue, 28 Jul 2026 21:03:10 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 251/254] reaper Warden v1.8.7: IPv6 dual-stack + top
 blocked-countries stats + full i18n

- rwarden.c: parallel IPv6 stack (hash:net family inet6 sets, ip6tables
  REAPER_WARDEN/RW_DROP chains, v6 CIDR validation, Spamhaus DROPv6 + ipdeny
  IPv6 country ranges, v6 anti-lockout for link-local/ULA/delegated prefix).
  Manual ban/allow entries auto-route v4/v6 by ':' detection.
- Per-country geo sets (rw_g_<cc>/rw_g6_<cc>) each with its own drop rule so
  the iptables packet counter attributes drops per country; generated stats.sh
  reads live iptables/ip6tables counters -> JSON (total + top countries).
- web.c: do_reaper_warden_cgi read-only stats endpoint (noMCP-safe, kept
  OUTSIDE the RTCONFIG_REAPER_MCP block), registered as reaper_warden.cgi.
- Reaper_Warden.asp: concise/professional wording (purpose + explicit
  not-a-sole-defense caveat, VPN/origin limits; caveat now dismissable),
  IPv4/IPv6 protocols tile, Blocked-hits tile, Top blocked countries card
  (live via reaper_warden.cgi, 30s refresh).
- i18n: full RWDN_ block (00-51) translated into all 24 languages (was
  English-seeded). Dicts lockstep 5842; reaper_langcheck 0 breakers.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
